  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "All tests pass now. The suite has two tests, and both pass.\n\n**The bug:** `src/vat.js` used `Math.floor(pence * 1.2)`, which truncates. The function's comment says the result should be \"rounded to the nearest penny\", and the failing test expects `withVat(999)` to be `1199`. Truncating `1198.8` gave `1198`.\n\n**The fix:** I changed `Math.floor` to `Math.round` on that one line. I didn't change the test. Half-pence values round up under `Math.round`, which matches the usual convention for prices.\n\nI haven't committed anything. The change is a single line in `src/vat.js`, and `git diff` will show it.",
